  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). You paste a Sanskrit sentence in any common script and get back a word segmentation that resolves sandhi and compounds, morphological tags for each word, dictionary and dhatu links, a syllable and phoneme breakdown, and the analysis rendered in a script you choose. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
